          "narration_script": "Building on what the CMS-485 is, let's discuss why the quality of your documentation directly drives our operational outcomes. It's easy to look at documentation as an administrative chore, but complete and traceable Plan of Care documentation has a profound impact on how smoothly our agency runs. First and foremost, high-quality documentation reduces claim rework. When the clinical story is clear the first time, we prevent avoidable Additional Development Requests—or ADRs—from escalating. That means less time chasing down signatures or rewriting rationales, and more time focusing on actual patient care. Furthermore, documentation isn't just for billers or auditors; it's a vital communication tool for our clinical team. A clear rationale for skilled care improves how our interdisciplinary teams execute the plan. It ensures that when a handoff occurs between a nurse and a physical therapist, the new clinician knows exactly what the goal is and why that skilled intervention is necessary. Ultimately, you should view documentation quality as serving a dual purpose: it is both a strict compliance control and a critical care-quality control. When we document thoroughly, we aren't just protecting our reimbursement—we are actively ensuring our patients receive safe, coordinated, and effective care.",
