          "completion_condition": "Learner views this card and continues.",
          "narration_script": "Staying within our regulatory framework, let's identify the specific content elements that must be present in every single Plan of Care. For the CMS-485 to be compliant, it must be complete, and every element must be traceable. First, we must be incredibly explicit. Every Plan of Care must clearly detail the patient's diagnoses, their measurable goals, the specific interventions planned, the disciplines involved, and the exact frequency and duration of the visits. There is simply no room for ambiguity. Second, we have to address the broader context of the patient's situation. When applicable, the plan must address safety risks, detail the support systems required for the patient's homebound status, and outline discharge planning. These aren't optional add-ons; they are core components of a holistic care plan. Why is this level of detail so critical? Because missing even one of these required elements can completely invalidate our medical necessity narrative. If a reviewer cannot trace your intervention back to a specific diagnosis or a measurable goal, they will question the necessity of the care. Missing elements inevitably lead to delayed and non-compliant billing. Ensuring every box is checked, and every narrative is complete, is how we secure our billing cycle.",
