          "display_title": "OASIS to Plan of Care Alignment",
          "learner_facing_content": "<p style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">Next, we move to a critical area of compliance: Clinical Alignment. Let’s focus specifically on aligning your OASIS assessment to the Plan of Care.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">The OASIS is the foundation of our clinical understanding of the patient, and it absolutely must be reflected in the strategy laid out in the Plan of Care. This is not a suggestion; it is a surveyor expectation. Every intervention listed on the Plan of Care should map directly back to an assessed deficit, a safety risk, or a clinical priority identified within the OASIS document.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">Contradictions between these two documents are massive red flags for reviewers. If your OASIS states the patient has a high risk for falls and severe mobility deficits, but your Plan of Care includes zero physical therapy and no fall-prevention interventions, you have created a glaring inconsistency. This alignment must be highly visible at the Start of Care, and equally important, it must be rigorously maintained through every single recertification period.</p>",
