          "narration_script": "Because diagnosis coding carries such high stakes, we must put strong Diagnosis Integrity Safeguards in place to reduce claim risk. How do we do this? First, we validate the logic of our chosen diagnoses against the actual visit content and the physician's orders before we finalize the code. We must actively avoid code selection driven by habit or history. Just because a patient had a primary diagnosis of heart failure last year does not mean it is the primary driver of their skilled need today. Our coding must reflect the patient's current, real-time clinical profile. Furthermore, if the principal diagnosis shifts across episodes—meaning the primary reason for home health changes from episode one to episode two—you must thoroughly document the clinical rationale for that shift. You cannot just quietly change the primary code without explaining to the auditor what physiological change occurred in the patient to justify the pivot.",
