          "completion_condition": "Learner views this card and continues.",
          "narration_script": "To close out our Audit Readiness section, let's look at the ultimate safeguard: The Pre-Bill Defensibility Checklist. This is our final line of defense to reduce avoidable exposure before a claim goes out the door. Before billing, every chart should pass these three specific checks: First, are all required signatures complete and correctly dated? Are all verbal and interim orders fully resolved and signed? Second, are all required Plan of Care elements present? Is the content highly patient-specific, and are the goals objectively measurable? And third, are the skilled need and homebound rationale explicit, detailed, and completely current based on the patient's most recent status? If the answer to any of these is no, the claim does not drop. Implementing and strictly adhering to this pre-bill checklist transforms audit readiness from a stressful, retrospective panic into a smooth, proactive daily habit.",
